# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets exclude list (gitignore syntax).
# These are build/deploy config, internal docs, and one-off dev/patch
# scripts that were previously being served publicly to anyone who
# browsed to their filename (e.g. yoursite.com/patch_admin.py).
wrangler.toml
_worker.js
firestore.rules
README.md
implementation_plan.md
*.py
test_*.html
test_*.js

# Git internals - were being served publicly (e.g. yoursite.com/.git/HEAD),
# which would let anyone pull the repo's commit history.
.git
.git/**

# Local wrangler dev/build artifacts - not meant to be public.
.wrangler
.wrangler/**

# Dependency and environment files - never meant to be public.
node_modules
node_modules/**
.env
.env.*
*.md
.DS_Store

# sops/ - the raw PDFs exported from ClickUp used to migrate content into
# the SOP Wiki tool (see sop-wiki/js/data.js, which has its own copy of
# this content as searchable text). Nothing in the app references this
# folder anymore, so it's dead deploy weight - and unlike the Wiki tool
# (gated behind Cloudflare Access + Hub sign-in), these were sitting here
# as directly-fetchable static files with zero access control, including
# genuinely sensitive ones (Cybersecurity Policy, Access & Login Log
# Template, Client Communication Policy, and more).
sops
sops/**

# One-off internal business documents that ended up at the repo root
# (pricing drafts, contractor agreement templates, planning docs) -
# never linked to or fetched by any tool, so there's no reason for these
# to be reachable as static files either.
*.docx
*.xlsx
Freelancer_Contractor_Agreement_Template.docx
Revital_Service_Pricing_Draft.xlsx
av_production_software_roadmap.pdf
business_phase_roadmap.pdf
where_to_log_what_hub_vs_clickup.pdf
Media Storage & Review Tools.pdf